  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender and Methodologies Virtual Platform Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project benefits social organisations working with gender perspective and on gender based violence prevention, facilitating a virtual space for reflection, and experiences and knowledge exchange. With this dynamic, they have methodological tools, broaden their theoretical-conceptual framework and strengthen their advocacy actions in favor of a more just and equal society, without gender based violence.
The project is aimed at civil society organizations, universities and social agents that promote changes towards gender equity in Central America (and LAC).
First, a Virtual Platform was installed. Second, the integration as active members was motivated to all those organizations that raised this initiative as an urgent need in the Central American Meeting &quot;Women and men walking towards gender equity&quot;, convened by Cantera in September 2017, among which are the member organizations of the Network for Equity and Gender Equality (RPEIG) of Nicaragua, different organizations that work on equity and non-violence in the country, organizations of the sister countries of Central America, counterparts of cooperation agencies that work at an intense level for gender equality and non-violence. CANTERA did enable the virtual space by sharing information about participating organizations and providing inputs to encourage dialogue, debate and reflection.
Once installed, webinars were promoted, as well as alliances at the local, national or regional level for mass dissemination of gender equality campaigns and the prevention of gender violence.
Third, it opened to other organizations or institutions interested in the subject to strengthen themselves more with the diversity of contributions, knowledge and experiences.
Since second half of 2022, the platform is managed by CEP-Alforja with former Cantera team members as consultants. 
This is CAC058 phase II and responds to the pathways for change stated at the CAFOD Central America regional strategy from 2023 onwards.</narrative>
  </description>
